## Pipeline / persistence
- Error-path `record_sync_run` — wrap `_full_build` in try/except, write `status=ERROR` row with the stack message; today only the SUCCESS path lands an audit row
- Open a RUNNING `sync_runs` row at dispatch start (so `WS /repos/{graph_id}/status` has something to stream); flip to SUCCESS/ERROR at end instead of single end-of-pipeline insert
- PATCH `_patch_sync`: git pull + `git diff --name-status -M`, load tree from `trees.tree_data`, run C4a/C4b on changed files only, mutate tree (drop changed-file nodes/edges, re-add from re-parse, fix cross-file edges), C5a rebuild, C5b partial re-cluster of affected communities only
- Repo cache eviction: TTL (7d idle) + LRU disk-budget; mark `repo_clones.evicted_at`, keep row as tombstone for re-clone

## API surface
- `GET /repos` — list authenticated user's graphs (needed for frontend list view)
- `GET /repos/{graph_id}/graph` — fetch clustered graph (blocker for frontend)
- `GET /trees/{tree_id}` — fetch indexed parse tree
- `DELETE /repos/{graph_id}` — explicit delete; cascades to `trees` + `sync_runs`
- `WS /repos/{graph_id}/status` — stream build progress from `sync_runs` row updates
- `POST /repos/{graph_id}/query` — C6 QnA endpoint
- Widen FastAPI exception handling — only `CloneError` / `ValueError` are mapped today; parse / Leiden / DB errors propagate as raw 500s

## Frontend (C7)
- Minimum-viable v1: react-force-graph-3d viewer, fetch graph by id, click-to-detail sidebar, served as static SPA from C1
- Defer for v1: auth flow, WebSocket build progress, QnA panel, semantic zoom — keep it small to validate the graph is actually useful

## QnA (C6)
- BFS 2-hop subgraph from query keywords (~2k tokens), `ClaudeSDKClient` single-shot, return answer with node references

## Auth
- `/auth/register`, `/auth/login`, JWT middleware
- Scope all `/repos` and `/trees` queries by `user_id` from JWT
- Drop the `_SYSTEM_USER_ID` placeholder in `graph_engine/utils/db_utils.py`
- Flip `tree.graph_id`, `graphs.user_id`, `repo_clones.user_id` to NOT NULL once every row is user-scoped

## Cleanup
- Remove `ENV=dev` fixture short-circuit in `hybrid_parsing/surgical_agent/resolver.py` once C4b is exercised end-to-end on real repos
- Frontend table in CLAUDE.md still says "WebGL force-graph (3d)"; pick 2D vs 3D when v1 lands and reconcile
